{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions","id":237585,"title":"Submissions","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scarred Lands"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-22T18:01:50-07:00","id":237585,"title":"Submissions","content":"Hi there. Great to see some Scarred Lands work appearing, particularly in pathfinder format. I've been working hard at pathfinder conversions for this great setting for some time; do you accept submissions and to whom would I send any work?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the path to never 'working' a day in my life","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3749-kplangers","name":"KPLangers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3749_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T18:22:20-07:00","id":237596,"title":"","content":"See the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/do-you-want-to-walk-the-onyx-path/\" target=\"_blank\">all-call</a><a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/do-you-want-to-walk-the-onyx-path/\" target=\"_blank\"> here</a> and the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/writer-all-call-follow-up/\" target=\"_blank\">followup here</a>. They don't mention <i>Scarred Lands</i>, because we weren't working on projects for it at the time, but they contain our process for submissions.<br /> <br /> Thanks for asking!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-22T22:53:58-07:00","id":237922,"title":"","content":"I have a related question, but as an artist rather than a writer.<br /> <br /> Is the Disclosure Form meant to be printed, signed and scanned, or filled out digitally and e-signed? I'm unable to access the Artist Disc. Form from the device I'm using, but I remember it having a bit more to it than the Writers form, including editability.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><br /> I draw things! Wanna check it out? Click on the link below!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.deviantart.com/jordantroy</a><br /> <br /> <i><b>YES! I do commissions! </b></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/848-jtroy","name":"JTroy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar848_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"183"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T07:11:56-07:00","id":238169,"title":"","content":"Am i getting it right and is Onyx Path going to publish revised/updated edition of the Scarred Lands setting, one compatible with Pathfinder's version of D20?<br /> <br /> Is that what this new forum area is about?<br /> <br /> I would like very much to see a new version of Scarn, specially one where the issue of divine might (are gods beings of unstatable, unreachable puisance or mighty, epic but limited beings? the setting danced in terribly contradicting ways around the issue a number of times), magic x psionics (gods x slarecians) and some points of power rituals and other setting-specific magic were given greater thought and some fine-tuning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T11:04:52-07:00","id":238352,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=238169#post238169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am i getting it right and is Onyx Path going to publish revised/updated edition of the Scarred Lands setting, one compatible with Pathfinder's version of D20?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not &quot;going to&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/133728?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\">Gauntlet of Spiragos</a> is already available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#800000\">Ian A. A. Watson</span></b><span style=\"color:#bdc3c7\">(he/she)</span><br /> <b>Onyx Path Community Manager<br /> Trinity Continuum Content Lead</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4-ianwatson","name":"IanWatson","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4_2.png","title":"Community Manager","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1512"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-23T21:19:30-07:00","id":238833,"title":"","content":"Oh I'm hyped. Just logged in and saw that there's new a Scarred Lands forum it! Scarred Lands was a wonderful setting, and I'm eager to see new material for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T07:39:38-07:00","id":239099,"title":"","content":"I've been a big fan of the game since the first book beat out the monster manual for 3rd edition. My only beef with the setting was the bizarre sense of scale each of the continents had themselves and compared to others in terms of their distance from one to another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/982-cptmachine","name":"Cptmachine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar982_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"44"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T01:40:09-07:00","id":240032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IanWatson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=238352#post238352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not &quot;going to&quot;.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/product/133728?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=TheOnyxPath\" target=\"_blank\">Gauntlet of Spiragos</a> is already available.</div> </div> </div> </div><img src=\"http://stickerish.com/wp-content/uploads/2011/04/AwwYeaWithText.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> Is all i have to say right now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T06:37:40-07:00","id":240225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cptmachine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=239099#post239099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been a big fan of the game since the first book beat out the monster manual for 3rd edition. My only beef with the setting was the bizarre sense of scale each of the continents had themselves and compared to others in terms of their distance from one to another.</div> </div> </div> </div> That's what teleportation magic is for no? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> With how rich and detailed the setting is, continents had to be on a grand scale to squeeze it all in I guess, plus a titan or 12 would need a huge playground. Most recently, the size has leant itself perfectly to a Kingmaker conversion I'm running on Ghelspad.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the path to never 'working' a day in my life","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3749-kplangers","name":"KPLangers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3749_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T17:55:36-07:00","id":240923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JTroy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=237922#post237922\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a related question, but as an artist rather than a writer.<br /> <br /> Is the Disclosure Form meant to be printed, signed and scanned, or filled out digitally and e-signed? I'm unable to access the Artist Disc. Form from the device I'm using, but I remember it having a bit more to it than the Writers form, including editability.</div> </div> </div> </div>The disclosure form is meant to be electronically signed, but we'll accept it as physically signed and scanned.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-03T23:28:55-07:00","id":272073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Cptmachine</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=239099#post239099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've been a big fan of the game since the first book beat out the monster manual for 3rd edition. My only beef with the setting was the bizarre sense of scale each the continents had themselves and compared to others in terms of their distance from one to another.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just think of Scarn as 90%+ water.<br /> <br /> I ran into similar problems with my game, but I considered it an awesome challenges to explain it all. Like, can you travel west from Ghelspad to get to Asherak? I decided no, and came up with a reason why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3993-ketina","name":"Ketina","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3993_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-10-04T01:19:23-07:00","id":272110,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ketina</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=272073#post272073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just think of Scarn as 90%+ water.<br /> <br /> I ran into similar problems with my game, but I considered it an awesome challenges to explain it all. Like, can you travel west from Ghelspad to get to Asherak? I decided no, and came up with a reason why.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm curious as to what exactly was your reason why one couldn't sail west from Ghelspad to Asherak. Just that Scarn's surface is primarily covered by water?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2630-mayberry","name":"Mayberry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2630_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-20T07:28:42-07:00","id":486348,"title":"","content":"I to am interested in doing some art. Here is my page, It even has some cover mock ups for scarred lands Net books i was planning on making eventually<br /> <a href=\"http://yardarkwood.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://yardarkwood.deviantart.com/gallery/</a>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5744-cliffrice","name":"CliffRice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-25T07:03:18-07:00","id":491610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm curious as to what exactly was your reason why one couldn't sail west from Ghelspad to Asherak. Just that Scarn's surface is primarily covered by water? </div> </div> </div>Actually, I don't think that it is state (anywhere) whether Scarn is actually a planet (like earth) or has another shape...<br /> <br /> Nice gallery CliffRice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T06:15:00-07:00","id":501626,"title":"","content":"Check out the Order of the Ancients picture which is a few pages into the Edge of Infinity supplement haaz, that might help to picture Scarn's shape <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>On the path to never 'working' a day in my life","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3749-kplangers","name":"KPLangers","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3749_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-03T07:25:09-07:00","id":501688,"title":"","content":"Well, that's a possibility (after that however, you have the dwarf that tells you that Scarn is an anvil, so you may think it's flat too). I would say the strongest argument for the spherical shape is in the map from the Blood Sea sourcebook (p16) which explicitly show a &quot;polar ice cap&quot;, which, I believe, can only be seen in a spherical world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Alain%20Giorla\" target=\"_blank\">Slarecian Vault contributions</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5793-haaz","name":"haaz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5793_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"66"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-04T22:48:13-07:00","id":503863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=491610#post491610\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I don't think that it is state (anywhere) whether Scarn is actually a planet (like earth) or has another shape...<br /> <br /> Nice gallery CliffRice <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5744-cliffrice","name":"CliffRice","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5744_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-06T16:59:13-07:00","id":506231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CliffRice</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=486348#post486348\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I to am interested in doing some art. Here is my page, It even has some cover mock ups for scarred lands Net books i was planning on making eventually<br /> <a href=\"http://yardarkwood.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://yardarkwood.deviantart.com/gallery/</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>I hope they can use some of your stuff, Cliff. <img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haaz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/scarred-lands/237585-submissions?p=501688#post501688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, that's a possibility (after that however, you have the dwarf that tells you that Scarn is an anvil, so you may think it's flat too). I would say the strongest argument for the spherical shape is in the map from the Blood Sea sourcebook (p16) which explicitly show a &quot;polar ice cap&quot;, which, I believe, can only be seen in a spherical world <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>They did say, in that book, that the different theories were intentionally contradictory.<br /> <br /> I have to say that, I would prefer to see Scarn being a spherical planet, that is in a &quot;solar system&quot; with several other planets. But, to play Devil's Advocate against my own preferred option, I don't think that a flatworld can be ruled out.<br /> <br /> I spent a bit of time studying Flat Earth theory recently (just to see if it could be used in a tabletop game). In that theory, they turn the North Pole into a single point in the middle of a flat circular disk, and they turn the South Pole into an ice wall that goes around the outside of the circular disc. (People argue against the mathematics that supports this theory, but that part of it works, if you accept it.)<br /> <br /> So Onyx Path could do a flatworld...or any other type of world, if they really wanted to.<br /> <br /> (One reason why I would prefer them to do a spherical world is that S&amp;SS never really made a big deal about the world being funky before, so it would seem like something bolted on at the last minute. And I say this as a Spelljammer fan who actually wants to see more funky worlds being published.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>David &quot;Big Mac&quot; Shepheard<br /> <i>Scarnspace is no longer the crystal sphere it once was. The celestial bodies bear horrible scars where gods felled titans. Many of the monstrous races that were created by the titans and gods during the war still survive in the gouged reaches of wildspace.</i><br /> You can see more of me at the <a href=\"http://www.thepiazza.org.uk/bb/viewforum.php?f=67\" target=\"_blank\">Scarred Lands forum at The Piazza</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5736-big-mac","name":"Big Mac","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5736_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}